PLZ110 hardware coexistence:
- For the observed HMA UID Fake 0.4.0+1c71b6c setuid inline hook, retain its
  entry, wrapper and original trampoline. After exact instruction, destination
  and CFI checks, redirect the native +4 resume body to our capability handler.
  No HMA code is copied or shipped; its unknown hook layouts remain rejected.
- src/health/userns.c is an original bounded boot check: drop to UID/GID 1000,
  create a user namespace, reject a host-root map, map the caller, reject host
  setns, and create a private UTS namespace. It does not change global policy.

FUSE boot-crash correction (v0.1.3):
- Native fuse_conn_init callers omit the unused user_ns argument when the host
  has CONFIG_USER_NS=n. Preserve their initial-namespace ownership instead of
  dereferencing that argument after enabling USER_NS in the LKM translation unit.
- Wrap fuse_get_tree with a checked native trampoline and reject noninitial
  fs_context owners with EOPNOTSUPP. FUSE's other inlined !USER_NS conversions
  are not yet ported, so sandbox-created FUSE mounts must not be assigned host
  ownership. Existing host FUSE mounts, including Android emulated storage,
  retain native behavior. New host mounts and teardown get explicit regressions.

Sandbox-created FUSE mounts (v0.1.4):
- live-fuse.c ports fuse_get_tree, parse/show options and child connection setup.
  Keep the checked native trampoline for host mounts and never read the unused
  native fuse_conn_init user_ns argument; assign the child owner explicitly.
- live-fuse-request.c ports request credential conversion, shares native request
  allocation/freeing, and wraps forced queueing for child UID/GID mappings.
- live-fuse-inode.c and live-fuse-dir.c port attribute, permission, setattr and
  creation paths whose CONFIG_USER_NS=n conversions were inlined by the host.
  Port fuse_do_getattr privately: the native static function drops its first
  parameter, so its compiled calling convention differs from its C prototype.
- live-fuse-acl.c ports FUSE/VFS ACL identity conversion for child FUSE only;
  native trampolines retain other filesystems' paths and existing LSM checks.
- Child connections reject Android FUSE-BPF backing/extra LOOKUP responses,
  no_daemon and fuseblk; mask passthrough/idmapped-mount INIT negotiation in
  both directions. Host connections retain native extension handling.
- Retain the original mount-owner, device-FD-owner and access checks, including
  allow_other namespace ancestry and native allow_sys_admin_access semantics.
